Show full contents of a documentation page

Displays the full markdown content of a page by its path. If the exact path is
not found, suggests similar pages.

This command prints text only. --json has no effect on it.

Usage: snouty docs show [OPTIONS] <PATH>

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          Page path (e.g. "product/writing_tests/controlling_faults")

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --offline
          Don't check for documentation updates

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
